        },
        {
          "name": "Official",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "This put the Shogun's government in a very awkward position. On one hand, the ronin had broken the law. They had planned a murder and carried out a private war in the capital.",
      "word_count": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-38",
      "section": "The verdict",
      "start": 466,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-38.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Townsman",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Townsman",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Townswoman",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "On the other hand, they had done exactly what the samurai code taught: total loyalty to their lord, even beyond death. Many people across Edo called them heroes.",
      "word_count": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-39",
      "section": "The verdict",
      "start": 478,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-39.png",
      "background": "palace",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Official",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "The government argued about it for weeks. In the end, it chose a compromise. The ronin would not be executed like criminals. Instead, they were allowed to die with honor, by seppuku.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-40",
